Review complete. `go vet` and `go test ./internal/` pass on the head; the refactor is behaviour-preserving in the paths I traced (provider ordering, log lines, `Run()` sequencing, the deleted test is a verbatim duplicate of `TestPublicGitLabRepositoryBackup`). No hard regressions found; the findings below are latent defects the refactor re-exposes or codifies in new shared helpers, plus cleanup the extracted helpers invite.

```json
[
  {
    "file": "internal/backup.go",
    "line": 228,
    "summary": "New shared helper logProviderBackupLFS gates on GetEnvOrFile (which honours *_FILE indirection) but then evaluates the flag with envTrue, which reads os.Getenv only, so the already-fetched value is discarded and _FILE-sourced values are never reported.",
    "failure_scenario": "Operator sets SOBA_GITHUB_BACKUP_LFS_FILE=/run/secrets/lfs containing 'true' and no plain env var: GetEnvOrFile returns ('true', true) but envTrue(envVar) sees os.Getenv=='' and returns false, so 'GitHub backup LFS: true' is silently omitted for all five providers that now route through this helper (same pattern on the GitHub skip-user-repos line at 251). Fix: parse the value returned by GetEnvOrFile instead of re-reading the environment."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/backup.go",
    "line": 277,
    "summary": "displayBitBucketStartupConfig still gates solely on SOBA_BITBUCKET_EMAIL even though the PR introduced bitbucketAPITokenDefined()/bitbucketOAuthDefined() and collectProviderBackupResults treats OAuth (user/key/secret) as a complete BitBucket configuration.",
    "failure_scenario": "BitBucket configured via SOBA_BITBUCKET_USER/KEY/SECRET with no email: backups for BitBucket run (collectProviderBackupResults accepts bitbucketOAuthDefined()), but startup prints no 'BitBucket backups to keep / compare method / backup LFS' lines, so the two code paths disagree about what counts as BitBucket being enabled. Gate on bitbucketAPITokenDefined() || bitbucketOAuthDefined() to reuse the new helpers consistently."
  },
